OL,3,GNEWSADress made for turn of the century
OL,4,Agoes on display
OL,5,
OL,6,FA dress designed to welcome in the 20th
OL,7,FCentury has gone on display for a month
OL,8,Fat a country house.
OL,10,FThe Cockleshell Dress was worn by Mary
OL,11,FVere Agar-Robartes, the eldest daughter
OL,12,Fof Thomas Charles Reginald
OL,13,FAgar-Robartes and Mary Dickinson, who
OL,14,Flived at Lanhydrock, near Bodmin,
OL,15,FCornwall, from 1879 to 1946.
OL,17,FThe dress - made from cream silk and
OL,18,Fdecorated with a shell pattern,
OL,19,Fgold-thread detailing and a
OL,20,Fcommemorative sash bearing the date
OL,21,F1900 - was restored by the National
OL,22,FTrust's textiles conservators.
OL,23,APub: 29-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
